 doesn\'t directly relate to the squirrel or the bear.\n7.**Rabbit likes the squirrel**: This tells us about the rabbit\'s relationship with the squirrel but not with the bear.\n8.**Rabbit sees the bear**: This means the rabbit has seen the bear.\n9.**Rabbit does not visit the bear**: This indicates that the rabbit has not visited the bear.\n10.**Rabbit visits the lion**: This tells us about the rabbit\'s relationship with the lion but not with the bear.\n11.**Squirrel visits the lion**: This indicates that the squirrel has visited the lion.\n12.**Squirrel sees the lion**: This means the squirrel has seen the lion.\n13.**Squirrel does not see the bear**: This is the statement we need to evaluate.The squirrel does not see the bear, and the rabbit does visit the bear. This provides clear information about the squirrel\'s relationship with the bear, contradicting the initial assumptions made.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
