ry is not cold, which we already know.).\n16.**If someone is smart then they are kind.** (This tells us Harry is kind.).\n17.**If someone is cold and round then they are smart.** (This tells us Harry is smart.).\n18.**If someone is kind and blue then they are big.** (This tells us Harry is big.).\n19.**Not all kind people are blue.** (This implies Harry is not blue.).\n20.**If someone is big then they are not nice.** (This implies Harry is not nice.).\n\nFrom the analysis, we can see that:.\n- Gary is big.\n- Gary is cold.\n- Harry is not blue.\n- Harry is not kind.\n- Harry is not nice.\n- All smart people are not round.\n- All nice people are not round.\n- If Harry is not cold then Harry is kind.\n- If someone is smart then they are not kind.\n- If someone is not cold or round then they are not smart.\n- If someone is not kind or blue then they are not big.\n- Not all kind people are blue.\n- If someone is big then they are not nice.\n\nSince Harry is not kind and blue, and not all kind people are blue, Harry must not be big. However, we also know that Gary is big. Therefore, Gary can be smart because if Gary were smart, he would not have to be kind and blue, which aligns with the fact that Gary is big.\n\nThus, the statement "Gary is smart" is true.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
