messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is nice. Bob is round. Bob is young. Dave is round. Erin is big. Erin is red. Gary is young. All round things are nice. All nice, big things are white. If something is big and white then it is round. Young things are nice. Big, red things are young. All nice things are quiet. All quiet things are big. Young, quiet things are red.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Gary is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, let\'s analyze each piece of information step by step:.\n\n1.**Bob is nice.Bob is round.Bob is young.** - This tells us that Bob is a nice, round, and young person.\n2.**Dave is round.** - This tells us that Dave is a round person.\n3.**Erin is big.Erin is red.** - This tells us that Erin is a big and red person.\n4.**Gary is young.** - This tells us that Gary is a young person.\n5.**All round things are nice.** - This means that if something is round, it is also nice.\n6.**All nice, big things are white.** - This means that if something is nice and big, it is also white.\n7.**If something is big and white then it is round.** - This means that if something is big and white, it must be round.\n8.**Young things are nice.** - This means that if something is young, it is also nice.\n9.**Big, red things are young.** - This means that if something is big and red, it is also young.\n10.**All nice things are quiet.** - This means that if something is nice, it is also quiet.\n11.According to the given information, Gary is not definitively big or red.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
