ans that if Gary is not furry, he must be hot. However, this does not directly apply to Bob because we do not know if he is furry.\n10.**If Bob is white then Bob is not smart.** - This means that if Bob is white, he must not be smart. However, we already know he is white, so this condition does not apply to Bob.\n11.**All cold, blue people are furry.** - This means that if someone is cold and blue, they are furry. However, this does not directly apply to Bob because we do not know if he is cold.\n\nBased on the analysis, we can conclude that Bob is not white and loud. Since we know that if someone is white then they are quiet, and we have no contradictory information about Bob\'s color or other attributes, the statement "Bob is loud" is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:.\nB) False.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
