messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Bob is big. Bob is furry. Bob is nice. Bob is rough. Bob is white. Bob is young. Erin is blue. Harry is nice. Harry is rough. Harry is white. Harry is young. If something is big then it is furry. If Erin is furry and Erin is white then Erin is blue. If something is furry and big then it is nice. If something is big then it is furry. If something is white and nice then it is rough. Furry, nice things are young. Furry, young things are white. All big, blue things are white. Young, blue things are nice.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Harry is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, let\'s analyze each piece of information step by step:.\n\n1.**Anne is big.** (This tells us that Anne is big.).\n2.**Bob is big.** (This tells us that Bob is big.).\n3.**Bob is furry.** (This tells us that Bob is furry.).\n4.**Bob is nice.** (This tells us that Bob is nice.).\n5.**Bob is rough.** (This tells us that Bob is rough.).\n6.**Bob is white.** (This tells us that Bob is white.).\n7.**Bob is young.** (This tells us that Bob is young.).\n8.**Erin is blue.** (This tells us that Erin is blue.).\n9.**Harry is nice.** (This tells us that Harry is nice.).\n10.**Harry is rough.** (This tells us that Harry is rough.).\n11.**Harry is white.** (This tells us that Harry is white.).\n12.**Harry is young.** (This tells us that Harry is young.).\n13.**If something is big then it is furry.** (This is a general rule.).\n14.**If Erin is furry and Erin is white then Erin is blue.** (This is a specific rule for Erin.).\n15.**If something is furry and big then it is nice.** (This is a general rule.).\n16.**If something is big then it is furry.** (This is a general rule.).\n17.**If something is white and nice then it is rough.** (This is a general rule.).Harry is not big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
