messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is furry. Bob is blue. Bob is green. Bob is young. Charlie is furry. Charlie is green. Charlie is red. Gary is furry. Gary is green. Gary is young. Furry, green things are blue. All big things are green. Red, furry things are blue. All big, blue things are nice. If Bob is nice and Bob is big then Bob is red. If Gary is furry then Gary is blue. All nice, big things are young. All nice things are young. Blue, young things are red.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is red.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Gary is red" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, let\'s analyze each piece of information step by step:.\n\n1.**Furry, green things are blue.**.\n   - This tells us that if something is both furry and green, it will be blue.\n\n2.**All big things are green.**.\n   - This means that if something is big, it will be green.\n\n3.**Red, furry things are blue.**.\n   - This tells us that if something is both red and furry, it will be blue.\n\n4.**All big, blue things are nice.**.\n   - This means that if something is both big and blue, it will be nice.\n\n5.**If Bob is nice and Bob is big then Bob is red.**.\n   - This tells us that if Bob is nice and big, then Bob must be red.\n\n6.**If Gary is furry then Gary is blue.**.\n   - This tells us that if Gary is furry, then Gary will be blue.\n\n7.**All nice, big things are young.**.\n   - This means that if something is both nice and big, it will be young.\n\n8.**All nice things are young.**.Gary is not red based on the given information.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
